# 15. Strategy Statistics

The system should calculate aggregated statistics.

At minimum:

```text
total executions
successful executions
failed executions
success rate
average quality
average confidence
average execution time
```

Statistics should be calculated per:

```text
strategy
task type
```

Example:

```text
calculation

direct_calculation
    success rate: 82%

verify_calculation
    success rate: 95%

step_by_step_calculation
    success rate: 88%
```

---

# 16. Strategy Comparison

Create a Strategy Comparison component.

It receives performance statistics for multiple strategies.

Example:

```text
Strategy A
Success: 82%

Strategy B
Success: 95%

Strategy C
Success: 88%
```

Result:

```text
Best Strategy:
Strategy B
```

The comparison MUST consider more than one metric where appropriate.

At minimum:

```text
correctness
quality
confidence
```

Execution time may be included as a secondary metric.

Correctness should have higher importance than speed.

---

# 17. Strategy Learning

After sufficient executions, the system should learn strategy preferences.

Example:

```text
Task Type: calculation

Best Strategy:
verify_calculation
```

This information must be persisted.

The learned preference should NOT overwrite the strategy definition.

Instead, maintain separate strategy-performance knowledge.

Conceptually:

```text
Strategy Definition
        +
Historical Performance
        +
Task Type
        ↓
Strategy Preference
```

---

# 18. Strategy Preference

Introduce a persistent strategy preference record.

Conceptually:

```text
strategy_preferences
--------------------
id
task_type
strategy_id
score
rank
confidence
sample_count
reason
updated_at
```

Example:

```text
task_type = calculation
strategy = verify_calculation
score = 0.95
rank = 1
confidence = high
sample_count = 20
```

---

# 19. Minimum Sample Requirement

The system MUST NOT declare a strategy as definitively superior after a single execution.

Introduce:

```text
STRATEGY_MIN_SAMPLES
```

Example:

```text
STRATEGY_MIN_SAMPLES=5
```

Until sufficient samples exist:

```text
Strategy status = insufficient_data
```

After sufficient data:

```text
Strategy status = evaluated
```

This prevents one lucky execution from permanently influencing strategy selection.

---

# 20. Cold Start

The system must handle a new strategy with no history.

Example:

```text
Strategy A
samples = 20
success = 95%

Strategy B
samples = 0
```

Strategy B must not automatically receive a poor score simply because it has no history.

The system should use the exploration mechanism to collect evidence.

