# 41. Phase 4 Acceptance Criteria

Phase 4 is complete when all of the following are true:

1. Multiple strategies can be registered.
2. The system can classify a task.
3. The system can select a strategy.
4. The selected strategy is recorded.
5. Strategy execution is recorded.
6. The answer is evaluated.
7. Strategy performance is persisted.
8. Multiple strategies can be compared.
9. The system can determine a preferred strategy.
10. Minimum sample requirements are enforced.
11. Cold-start strategies are supported.
12. Exploration is supported.
13. Future requests can use learned strategy preferences.
14. Strategy information survives application restart.
15. GraphQLite contains strategy relationships.
16. Streamlit displays strategy information.
17. ADK Web remains the primary agent interface.
18. All tests pass.
19. Strategy optimization failures do not break normal answers.
20. No source code or prompt self-modification occurs.

